  "_README": "Royal-name lexicon for cartouche correction (cartouche_matcher.py). Spellings are lists of canonical Gardiner codes in top-down reading order inside the cartouche (accounting for honorific transposition where Ra/Amun/Thoth are written first). Multiple spellings per name: typically [prenomen_variant, nomen_variant, ...]. Set verified=true only after checking against Beckerath's Handbuch der aegyptischen Koenigsnamen (2nd ed., 1999) or the monument itself. Unverified entries still match but are flagged in the result. Generated 2026-06-25 -- ALL new entries need validation. Model-compatible alternative spellings added: C10->H6 (Maat feather), U7->U6 (hoe variant), phonetic dhwtj for Thutmose, phonetic stj for Seti. Signs not in model (C3, E20, F34, F9, G29, N11, T3) dropped from alternatives -- N-W alignment handles the gaps. 2026-11-11: spelling_names is parallel to spellings and says which name each spelling writes (kind throne or birth, and its transliteration), so the matcher labels a throne-name cartouche as the throne name. Kings without it have one name and keep the plain translit.",
